@startuml campusclaw_failure_boundary

title Failure Logging: Record Cause, Return Stable Code
autonumber
hide footbox
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam maxMessageSize 190
skinparam BoxPadding 10
skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor #475569
  LifeLineBorderColor #94A3B8
  ParticipantBorderColor #64748B
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
  GroupBorderColor #94A3B8
  GroupBackgroundColor #F1F5F9
}

actor Caller
boundary "Public boundary\nHTTP / SSE" as Public
control "Failure source" as Source
database "Service log\nSLF4J / ECS" as Log

== 1. Identify failure at its source ==
Caller -> Public : Invoke operation
Public -> Source : Execute
alt Original Throwable exists
  Source -> Log : Own Logger: code, safe context, cause
else Deterministic validation or state rejection
  Source -> Source : Choose stable code\nNo synthetic exception log
end

== 2. Cross the boundary with a code-only carrier ==
alt Synchronous Runtime failure
  Source --> Public : RuntimeApiException(errorCode)
  Public --> Caller : HTTP status + controlled response
else Mate streaming failure
  Source --> Public : AssistantMessage(errorCode)\nerrorMessage = null
  Public --> Caller : Existing stream.error
end

== 3. Process-level failures ==
opt Startup failure (separate entry point)
  Source -> Log : STARTUP_FAILED and original cause
  Source --> Caller : StartupException(errorCode)
end

legend bottom left
Source constructs the code-only carrier after logging.
Exception cause is null; writable stack trace is disabled.
No payloads, credentials, headers, upstream resMsg, or raw SSE in logs.
Public boundaries do not log the same code-only business failure again.
endlegend
@enduml
